# Copy to deploy/.env (or export in the shell). Never commit real secrets.
# Used by: docker compose overlays, Caddy, backup/restore helpers.

# --- JWT_SECRET ---
# Meaning: HS256 signing key for Bearer JWTs. Required in production / compose
# (fail-closed; see docker-compose.yml and src/server/auth.ts).
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=

# --- DOMAIN ---
# Meaning: public DNS base name. Caddy serves api.$DOMAIN (and optional mcp.$DOMAIN).
# Placeholder only in-repo — replace with your hostname (free DDNS OK).
# Example: example.com
DOMAIN=example.com

# --- ACME_EMAIL ---
# Meaning: contact email for Let's Encrypt / ACME via Caddy.
# Generate: use a real mailbox you control (placeholder below is not a secret).
# Example: admin@example.com
ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# --- ALLOW_DEMO_TOKENS ---
# Meaning: when 1, opaque demo Bearers (customer-token, merchant-token, …) work.
# Production / public deploys MUST keep 0. Local demos only: set 1.
# Generate: N/A — boolean flag; default 0.
ALLOW_DEMO_TOKENS=0

# --- Optional ops ---
# Compose project name affects Docker volume names used by backup.sh / restore.sh.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=agent-commerce
#
# Backup retention count for deploy/backup.sh (default 7).
# BACKUP_RETAIN=7
#
# Grafana admin password when using deploy/docker-compose.observability.yml
# (change from default; not a repo secret — set locally).
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin
